commands-help-drawing-brush = Return to the last drawing brush.
commands-help-sculpt = Return to the last sculpting tool.
commands-help-pen = Use the last brush selected in this tool family.
commands-help-clone = Paint with pixels copied from the source disc; Set Source picks its spot. With Reference layers it copies the marked layers below the editing layer and the editing layer itself, while Wand and Fill sample every marked layer.
commands-help-heal = Paint with pixels copied from the source disc, like the Clone Stamp. When you lift the pen, the copy takes on the color and brightness around the stroke while keeping its texture.
commands-help-spot-heal = Paint over a spot or blemish. When you lift the pen, it is replaced with texture from the most similar nearby area, blended into its surroundings. It matches by proximity only; Content-Aware and Create Texture aren't available.
commands-help-select = Return to the last selection tool.
commands-help-selection-brush = Paint the area that subsequent edits will affect.
commands-help-selection-intersect = Keep only the area shared by the existing and new selections.
commands-help-selection-visible = Find matching colors across the visible artwork.
commands-help-selection-editing = Sample the editing layer only: selection tools find colors in it, and retouching copies from it.
commands-help-selection-reference = Sample layers marked as references; retouching copies the ones below the editing layer with the editing layer over them.
commands-help-selection-fixed-ratio = Keep the selection's width-to-height ratio fixed.
commands-help-selection-fixed-size = Use the configured selection width and height.
commands-help-quick-mask = Edit the selection as a painted mask.
commands-help-reselect = Restore the previous pixel selection.
commands-help-save-selection-layer = Keep the current selection as a reusable selection layer.
commands-help-move = Move artwork and manage image placement on the canvas.
commands-help-scale-rotate = Resize or rotate the current transform target.
commands-help-fit-canvas = Adjust the zoom to show the entire canvas.
commands-help-actual-pixels = Zoom to 100% so each image pixel covers one screen pixel.
commands-help-flip-horizontal = Mirror the view without changing the artwork.
commands-help-rotate-left = Rotate the view without changing the artwork.
commands-help-undo-workspace = Restore the previous toolbar, panel or workspace layout.
commands-help-redo-workspace = Reapply an undone workspace layout change.
commands-help-zen-mode = Hide or restore workspace controls to give the canvas more room.
commands-help-show-canvas-action-bar = Show next steps beside selections, transforms and placed images.
commands-help-transform-flip-horizontal = Mirror the content being transformed, about the centre of its box.
commands-help-transform-rotate-left = Turn the content being transformed by a quarter turn.
commands-help-reset-transform = Undo every change made in this transform, keeping it open.
commands-help-remove-selection-point = Remove the most recent point of a polygon selection in progress.
commands-help-mask-selection = Add or replace the active layer's mask so only the selection shows.
commands-help-transform-free = Transform with box handles; Uniform keeps proportions.
commands-help-transform-distort = Pin each corner of the transform box independently, including perspective.
commands-help-transform-perspective = While distorting, mirror each corner drag onto its neighbour for symmetric perspective.
commands-help-transform-nearest = Choose how transformed pixels are resampled: hard-edged, smooth, smooth and sharp, or with the most detail.
commands-help-transform-warp = Bend the content with a mesh of curved patches, dragging its nodes and their tangent handles.
commands-help-warp-grid-three = Choose how many patches the warp mesh has, keeping its current shape.
commands-help-use-reference-below = Mark the nearest visible photo or paint layer below as a reference for Wand and Fill.
commands-help-clone-source-arm = Pick where retouching copies from: the next pen or mouse click sets the source.
commands-help-clone-aligned = Keep one offset between the source and the brush across strokes; when off, every stroke starts copying at the source disc.
commands-help-clone-flip-horizontal = Mirror the copied pixels about the source disc.
commands-help-clone-reset-offset = Start the next stroke copying at the source disc again.
commands-help-clear-layer = Erase everything on the active layer. A placed photo's original is discarded too.
commands-help-clear-selected = Erase the selected pixels of the active layer; soft edges erase partially. A placed photo keeps its original.
commands-help-clear-outside = Erase the pixels of the active layer outside the selection.
commands-help-copy-selection-to-layer = Copy the selected pixels to a new layer above, in place. Without a selection, duplicate the layer.
commands-help-cut-selection-to-layer = Move the selected pixels from the active layer to a new layer above, in place.
commands-help-revert-to-original = Discard painting, erasing and applied masks on a placed photo, keeping its placement, mask, opacity and blend mode.
commands-help-merge-down = Merge the active layer into the layer below. A clipping base merges its clipped layers, and an effect layer applies to the layer below only. Placed photos become document pixels.
commands-help-merge-group = Merge the active group into one layer with the group's blend mode and opacity, discarding its hidden layers. Placed photos become document pixels.
commands-help-merge-visible = Merge every visible layer into one, keeping hidden layers. Placed photos become document pixels.
commands-help-flatten-image = Merge every visible layer into one over the paper and discard hidden layers and pixels outside the canvas. Placed photos become document pixels.
commands-help-stamp-visible = Add a layer on top with everything visible merged into it, keeping every layer.
commands-help-blend-perceptual = Combine layers on the document's encoded values, as Photoshop and Clip Studio Paint do. Painted pixels keep their values.
commands-help-blend-linear = Combine layers in linear light, which is physically based. Painted pixels keep their values.
commands-help-load-selection-layer = Use the Selection Layer being edited as the current selection and return to the artwork.
commands-help-invert-selection-layer = Invert the stored coverage of the Selection Layer being edited, staying in the mode.
commands-help-invert-layer-mask = Swap what the active layer's mask shows and hides.
commands-help-layer-mask-enabled = Turn the active layer's mask on or off without changing it.
commands-help-apply-layer-mask = Erase the pixels the active layer's mask hides, then remove the mask.
commands-help-edit-layer-mask = Paint on the active layer's mask instead of its pixels.
commands-help-edit-layer-content = Leave mask editing and paint on the active layer's pixels.
commands-help-lasso-fill = Draw a freehand shape filled with the drawing color.
commands-help-canvas-size = Set the canvas size from an anchor, in pixels or percent. Layers keep pixels outside the canvas, so a smaller canvas can grow back.
commands-help-crop-canvas-to-selection = Shrink the canvas to the selection's bounds. Pixels outside stay on their layers, hidden until the canvas grows again.
commands-help-grow-selection = Expand the selection, Quick Mask or edited Selection Layer by a distance, keeping soft values.
commands-help-shrink-selection = Contract the selection, Quick Mask or edited Selection Layer by a distance, keeping soft values.
commands-help-feather-selection = Soften the edges of the selection, Quick Mask or edited Selection Layer with a Gaussian blur.
commands-help-border-selection = Replace the selection with a band of the chosen width along its edge.
commands-help-smooth-selection = Fill notches and remove spikes narrower than twice the radius, keeping the canvas edges.
commands-help-transform-selection-outline = Move, scale, rotate or flip the selection outline; the pixels stay where they are.
commands-help-crop = Drag the crop handles, choose a ratio or straighten, then apply. Cropped pixels stay hidden on their layers unless Delete Cropped Pixels is on; dragging past the canvas adds transparent canvas.
commands-help-crop-swap-orientation = Swap the crop between landscape and portrait.
commands-help-crop-cycle-overlay = Show the next crop guide: thirds, grid, diagonal or golden ratio.
commands-help-crop-straighten = Draw a line along something that should be level or upright; the crop turns to match.
commands-help-crop-delete-cropped-pixels = Discard the pixels outside the crop when it is applied, instead of keeping them hidden. Placed photos keep their original.
commands-help-straighten-to-guide = Start a crop turned level with the selected straight guide.
commands-help-crop-fit-content = Set the crop to the bounds of the visible pixels, including those beyond the canvas.
commands-help-image-size = Scale the whole image to a new size in pixels or percent, or change only its resolution. Paint layers are resampled; placed photos keep their original pixels.
commands-help-rotate-image-left = Turn the whole image, with its selection and guides. Pixels move without resampling.
commands-help-flip-image-horizontal = Mirror the whole image, with its selection and guides. Pixels move without resampling.
commands-help-trim = Shrink the canvas to the visible pixels, removing transparent edges. Pixels outside stay on their layers, hidden.
commands-help-reveal-all = Grow the canvas to show every layer's pixels, including hidden layers and pixels outside the canvas.
commands-help-move-leave-copy = When Move drags selected pixels, place a copy and keep the original in place. Holding Alt as the drag starts does the opposite.
commands-help-copy = Copy the active layer's own pixels within the selection, before its opacity, mask and effects. Without a selection, copy the whole layer within the canvas.
commands-help-cut = Copy the active layer's selected pixels, then erase them from the layer.
commands-help-copy-merged = Copy the visible image within the selection, as an export would show it.
commands-help-paste-image = Add the clipboard as a new layer. A copy from Capy Canvas keeps its position when that is in view; an image from another app opens with placement handles.
commands-help-paste-in-place = Add the clipboard as a new layer where it was copied from, with no placement handles. An image from another app is centred at full size.
commands-help-paste-into = Add the clipboard where it was copied from, as a new layer whose mask shows only the selection.
commands-help-new-dodge-burn-layer = Add a Soft Light layer of neutral gray above the active layer. Paint on it in white to lighten and in black to darken.
commands-help-frequency-separation = Split the active layer into Low, its colors and tones blurred to a radius, and High, its fine texture, in a new group. The layer stays below, hidden.
commands-help-color-mix-oklab = Choose how this brush mixes the colors it picks up: Oklab blends evenly as the eye sees color, Linear light blends as light does, and Classic blends like Clip Studio Paint.
commands-cycle-through-tools-in-this-family = Cycle through tools in this family.
